      "writtenOn": "2026-04-17T21:34:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about this: instead of a CompletionData variant we have a `std::optional\u003cQueueAndSerial\u003e` and a `std::atomic\u003cbool\u003e` always present.\n\n`IsReadyToComplete` first checks the atomic - if it\u0027s true we just return that. Otherwise, if the `QueueAndSerial` is present, it checks that instead and sets the atomic to true if the queue serial has completed.\n\n`SetReadyToComplete` first sets the atomic. Then if the QueueAndSerial is present, it just sets that to nullopt (not strictly necessary actually).\n\nSo in essence all events have one source of truth for completion state which is the atomic.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 168,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 168,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "b5794001985e841801134968aef2c7ac1c7e41c1",
